12|🔴 T1 Data Analysis Foundations|Tablea.how_it_works:
**Basic calculated field**: evaluated row by row before aggregation
```
// Profit margin per order
Profit Margin = SUM([Profit]) / SUM([Sales])

// Days to ship
Days to Ship = DATEDIFF('day', [Order Date], [Ship Date])

// Customer tier using IF
Customer Tier = IF [Revenue] > 10000 THEN 'VIP'
               ELSEIF [Revenue] > 1000 THEN 'Regular'
               ELSE 'Low' END
```

**LOD (Level of Detail) expressions**:
```
// FIXED: compute at a specified grain, ignoring view filters except context filters
// Average sales per customer, regardless of what's on the view
{FIXED [Customer ID] : AVG([Sales])}

// INCLUDE: compute at view grain + specified field
// Sales per customer within each region (view is at region level)
{INCLUDE [Customer ID] : SUM([Sales])}

// EXCLUDE: compute at view grain MINUS the specified field
// Category total sales (excludes Sub-Category even if it's in the view)
{EXCLUDE [Sub-Category] : SUM([Sales])}

// % of category total (using FIXED)
Sales % of Category = SUM([Sales]) / SUM({FIXED [Category] : SUM([Sales])})
```

**FIXED {FIXED [dim1, dim2, ...] : AGG([measure])}**:
Computes the aggregate at the specified dimensions. Ignores all view-level dimension filters (except context filters and data source filters).

```
// Max sales per customer, available as a row-level value even in a region-level view
{FIXED [Customer ID] : MAX([Sales])}

// Average order value per region (fixed at region, ignores sub-region in view)
{FIXED [Region] : AVG([Sales])}
```

**INCLUDE {INCLUDE [dim] : AGG([measure])}**:
Adds the specified dimension to the current view dimensions for this calculation.

```
// In a view by Category: compute avg sales per customer within category
// Include adds Customer ID to Category: aggregates at Category×Customer level, then avg
{INCLUDE [Customer ID] : AVG([Sales])}
```

**EXCLUDE {EXCLUDE [dim] : AGG([measure])}**:
Removes a dimension from the view for this calculation.

```
// In a view by Category > Sub-Category: get Category-level total ignoring Sub-Category
{EXCLUDE [Sub-Category] : SUM([Sales])}
// Now: SUM(Sales) / {EXCLUDE [Sub-Category] : SUM(Sales)} = % of category total
```

**Filter precedence** (strongest to weakest):
Data Source Filters > Context Filters > FIXED LOD > Dimension Filters > INCLUDE/EXCLUDE LOD > Table Calculations

